IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa-definitions`
IMPORT `coa6-private-and-public`

-- coa6-tests-private-and-public.l4: tests of coa6-private-and-public.l4 (ss 270 to 273).
-- Every expected value was decided by reading the text of the section (line numbers in the comments are of ukpga-2006-46.txt)
-- before the encoding was run, and is written beside its assertion. A failing assertion is a finding, never an edit.
-- The pounds used for "level 4" and "level 5" below are ILLUSTRATIONS: the Act does not say what a level stands for.
--
-- Reading the answers: JUST TRUE is the text's yes, JUST FALSE the text's no in its own words, NOTHING "not covered".

§ `Tests: ss 270 to 273`

-- ---- the keel's s 4 wired to the seams (a private company and a public company, built from facts) -------------------------

`s 270 test a private company profile` MEANS `Company profile` WITH
    `place of registration` IS `England and Wales`
    `liability of the members` IS `liability limited to the amount, if any, unpaid on the shares held`
    `a share capital` IS FALSE
    `certificate of incorporation stating that it is a public company` IS FALSE

`s 270 test a public company profile` MEANS `Company profile` WITH
    `place of registration` IS `England and Wales`
    `liability of the members` IS `liability limited to the amount, if any, unpaid on the shares held`
    `a share capital` IS TRUE
    `certificate of incorporation stating that it is a public company` IS TRUE

-- s 4(1), s 4(2) (the keel): a company whose certificate does not say "public" is private, and conversely.
#ASSERT `s 4(1) the company is a private company` `s 270 test a private company profile` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(2) the company is a public company` `s 270 test a public company profile` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 270(1) says no for the keel's private company ("A private company is not required to have a secretary") ...
#ASSERT `s 270(1) the private company is required to have a secretary` (`s 4(1) the company is a private company` `s 270 test a private company profile` TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- ... and is silent for the keel's public company (s 270(1) speaks of a private company only).
#ASSERT `s 270(1) the private company is required to have a secretary` (`s 4(1) the company is a private company` `s 270 test a public company profile` TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 271 says yes for the keel's public company and is silent for the private one.
#ASSERT `s 271 the public company must have a secretary` (`s 4(2) the company is a public company` `s 270 test a public company profile` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 271 the public company must have a secretary` (`s 4(2) the company is a public company` `s 270 test a private company profile` TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- s 270(1) --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- (1) "A private company is not required to have a secretary."
#ASSERT `s 270(1) the private company is required to have a secretary` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 270(1) the private company is required to have a secretary` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 270(1) the private company is required to have a secretary` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- s 270(2) --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- (2) "without a secretary" is a private company that for the time being is taking advantage of the exemption (has none);
-- "with a secretary" "shall be construed accordingly".
#ASSERT `s 270(2) the company is a private company without a secretary` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 270(2) the company is a private company without a secretary` (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 270(2) the company is a private company without a secretary` (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 270(2) the company is a private company without a secretary` NOTHING FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 270(2) the company is a private company with a secretary` (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 270(2) the company is a private company with a secretary` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 270(2) the company is a private company with a secretary` (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 270(2) the company is a private company with a secretary` NOTHING TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- s 270(3)(a)(i): things to be sent to the secretary may go to the company itself -----------------------------------------
-- arguments: private?, has a secretary?, thing is of kind (a)?
#ASSERT `s 270(3)(a)(i) the thing may be given or sent to, or served on, the company itself` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a thing that is not of the kind (a) describes is outside the limb
#ASSERT `s 270(3)(a)(i) the thing may be given or sent to, or served on, the company itself` (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- a private company WITH a secretary is outside "In the case of a private company without a secretary": JUST FALSE (name-test sweep, group (i))
#ASSERT `s 270(3)(a)(i) the thing may be given or sent to, or served on, the company itself` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was `#ASSERT `s 270(3)(a)(i) the thing may be given or sent to, or served on, the company itself` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING`; name-test sweep, group (i): the gate "In the case of a private company without a secretary" is the text's own, so outside it the answer is JUST FALSE, not flipped to NOTHING
-- a public company is outside it too: JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 270(3)(a)(i) the thing may be given or sent to, or served on, the company itself` (JUST FALSE) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was `#ASSERT `s 270(3)(a)(i) the thing may be given or sent to, or served on, the company itself` (JUST FALSE) FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING`; name-test sweep, group (i): the gate "In the case of a private company without a secretary" is the text's own, so outside it the answer is JUST FALSE, not flipped to NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 270(3)(a)(i) the thing may be given or sent to, or served on, the company itself` NOTHING FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- s 270(3)(a)(ii): "if addressed to the secretary shall be treated as addressed to the company" ---------------------------
-- arguments: private?, has a secretary?, thing is of kind (a)?, addressed to the secretary?
#ASSERT `s 270(3)(a)(ii) the thing addressed to the secretary is treated as addressed to the company` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 270(3)(a)(ii) the thing addressed to the secretary is treated as addressed to the company` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 270(3)(a)(ii) the thing addressed to the secretary is treated as addressed to the company` (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 270(3)(a)(ii) the thing addressed to the secretary is treated as addressed to the company` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 270(3)(a)(ii) the thing addressed to the secretary is treated as addressed to the company` (JUST FALSE) FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 270(3)(a)(ii) the thing addressed to the secretary is treated as addressed to the company` NOTHING FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- s 270(3)(b): anything else done by or to the secretary may be done by or to a director or an authorised person ------------
-- arguments: private?, has a secretary?, thing required or authorised to be done by or to the secretary?, thing is of kind (a)?,
--            the person is a director (s 250)?, the person is authorised by the directors?
-- (i) a director
#ASSERT `s 270(3)(b) the thing may be done by or to the person` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (ii) a person authorised generally or specifically by the directors (not a director)
#ASSERT `s 270(3)(b) the thing may be done by or to the person` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE FALSE (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (ii) holds even when whether the person is a director is not settled
#ASSERT `s 270(3)(b) the thing may be done by or to the person` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE FALSE NOTHING TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- neither limb: the list is not closed with "only", so the answer is not covered
#ASSERT `s 270(3)(b) the thing may be done by or to the person` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 270(3)(b) the thing may be done by or to the person` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE FALSE NOTHING FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- "anything else": a thing of kind (a) is not within (b)
#ASSERT `s 270(3)(b) the thing may be done by or to the person` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- a thing not required or authorised to be done by or to the secretary is not within (b)
#ASSERT `s 270(3)(b) the thing may be done by or to the person` (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- a private company with a secretary, or a public company, is outside "In the case of a private company without a secretary": JUST FALSE (group (i))
#ASSERT `s 270(3)(b) the thing may be done by or to the person` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was `#ASSERT `s 270(3)(b) the thing may be done by or to the person` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING`; name-test sweep, group (i): the gate "In the case of a private company without a secretary" is the text's own, so outside it the answer is JUST FALSE, not flipped to NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 270(3)(b) the thing may be done by or to the person` (JUST FALSE) FALSE TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was `#ASSERT `s 270(3)(b) the thing may be done by or to the person` (JUST FALSE) FALSE TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING`; name-test sweep, group (i): the gate "In the case of a private company without a secretary" is the text's own, so outside it the answer is JUST FALSE, not flipped to NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 270(3)(b) the thing may be done by or to the person` NOTHING FALSE TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- s 271 -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- "A public company must have a secretary."
#ASSERT `s 271 the public company must have a secretary` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 271 the public company must have a secretary` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 271 the public company must have a secretary` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 272(1) calls not having one "in breach of section 271": arguments: public?, has a secretary?
#ASSERT `s 271 the public company is in breach of section 271` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 271 the public company is in breach of section 271` (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 271 the public company is in breach of section 271` (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 271 the public company is in breach of section 271` NOTHING FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- s 272(1) ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- arguments: public?, it appears to the Secretary of State that the company is in breach of section 271?
#ASSERT `s 272(1) the Secretary of State may give the company a direction under section 272` (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a power: where it does not appear to the Secretary of State, or the company is not public, the text is not answered (NOTHING, never FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 272(1) the Secretary of State may give the company a direction under section 272` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 272(1) the Secretary of State may give the company a direction under section 272` (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 272(1) the Secretary of State may give the company a direction under section 272` NOTHING TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- s 272(2): the content of the direction --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- arguments: states the company appears to be in breach?, specifies what to do?, specifies the period?
#ASSERT `s 272(2) the direction states and specifies what the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 272(2) the direction states and specifies what the subsection requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 272(2) the direction states and specifies what the subsection requires` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 272(2) the direction states and specifies what the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- (2), closing words: "not less than one month or more than three months after the date on which the direction is given".
-- A direction given on 15 March 2024: one month after is 15 April 2024, three months after is 15 June 2024.
#ASSERT `s 272(2) the period specified is not less than one month or more than three months after the date the direction is given` (Date 15 3 2024) (Date 14 4 2024) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 272(2) the period specified is not less than one month or more than three months after the date the direction is given` (Date 15 3 2024) (Date 15 4 2024) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 272(2) the period specified is not less than one month or more than three months after the date the direction is given` (Date 15 3 2024) (Date 1 5 2024) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 272(2) the period specified is not less than one month or more than three months after the date the direction is given` (Date 15 3 2024) (Date 15 6 2024) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 272(2) the period specified is not less than one month or more than three months after the date the direction is given` (Date 15 3 2024) (Date 16 6 2024) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A direction given on 31 January 2023: the month after has no 31st, so one month after is taken as 28 February 2023 and three
-- months after as 30 April 2023 (fork F-months in NOTES.md).
#ASSERT `s 272(2) the period specified is not less than one month or more than three months after the date the direction is given` (Date 31 1 2023) (Date 27 2 2023) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 272(2) the period specified is not less than one month or more than three months after the date the direction is given` (Date 31 1 2023) (Date 28 2 2023) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 272(2) the period specified is not less than one month or more than three months after the date the direction is given` (Date 31 1 2023) (Date 30 4 2023) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 272(2) the period specified is not less than one month or more than three months after the date the direction is given` (Date 31 1 2023) (Date 1 5 2023) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ---- s 272(3) --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#ASSERT `s 272(3) the direction informs the company of the consequences of failing to comply` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 272(3) the direction informs the company of the consequences of failing to comply` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ---- s 272(4) and (5): the duty to comply ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#ASSERT `s 272(4) the company must comply with the direction by making the appointment and giving notice of it` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 272(4) the company must comply with the direction by making the appointment and giving notice of it` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 272(5) the company must comply with the direction by giving notice of the appointment` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 272(5) the company must comply with the direction by giving notice of the appointment` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- A direction given on 15 March 2024 specifies a period ending on 15 May 2024 (two months: inside the limits).
-- One step, "before the end of the period specified in the direction" (arguments: the day done, the last day, the day of the question):
-- on the last day is in time; one day after is not; not done yet is open while the period runs and a failure once it has ended.
#ASSERT `s 272(4) the step was taken before the end of the period specified in the direction` (JUST (Date 20 3 2024)) (Date 15 5 2024) (Date 21 3 2024) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 272(4) the step was taken before the end of the period specified in the direction` (JUST (Date 15 5 2024)) (Date 15 5 2024) (Date 16 5 2024) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 272(4) the step was taken before the end of the period specified in the direction` (JUST (Date 16 5 2024)) (Date 15 5 2024) (Date 17 5 2024) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 272(4) the step was taken before the end of the period specified in the direction` NOTHING (Date 15 5 2024) (Date 10 5 2024) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 272(4) the step was taken before the end of the period specified in the direction` NOTHING (Date 15 5 2024) (Date 15 5 2024) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 272(4) the step was taken before the end of the period specified in the direction` NOTHING (Date 15 5 2024) (Date 16 5 2024) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Both steps (JUST FALSE if either is, JUST TRUE if both are, else NOTHING).
#ASSERT `s 272(4) both steps` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 272(4) both steps` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 272(4) both steps` (JUST FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 272(4) both steps` NOTHING (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 272(4) both steps` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 272(4) both steps` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 272(4) both steps` NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

-- Has the company complied? arguments: in breach of s 271?, appointment already made?, day appointment made, day notice given,
-- last day of the period, day of the question.
-- (4): in breach, so BOTH the appointment and the notice, before the end of the period.
#ASSERT `s 272(4)-(5) the company has complied with the direction` TRUE FALSE (JUST (Date 20 3 2024)) (JUST (Date 25 3 2024)) (Date 15 5 2024) (Date 26 3 2024) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 272(4)-(5) the company has complied with the direction` TRUE FALSE (JUST (Date 15 5 2024)) (JUST (Date 15 5 2024)) (Date 15 5 2024) (Date 16 5 2024) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- appointment made, notice not yet given, the period still running: not yet decided
#ASSERT `s 272(4)-(5) the company has complied with the direction` TRUE FALSE (JUST (Date 1 5 2024)) NOTHING (Date 15 5 2024) (Date 10 5 2024) EQUALS NOTHING
-- appointment made, notice never given, the period over: not complied
#ASSERT `s 272(4)-(5) the company has complied with the direction` TRUE FALSE (JUST (Date 1 5 2024)) NOTHING (Date 15 5 2024) (Date 16 5 2024) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- neither done, the period over
#ASSERT `s 272(4)-(5) the company has complied with the direction` TRUE FALSE NOTHING NOTHING (Date 15 5 2024) (Date 16 5 2024) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- neither done, the period running
#ASSERT `s 272(4)-(5) the company has complied with the direction` TRUE FALSE NOTHING NOTHING (Date 15 5 2024) (Date 1 4 2024) EQUALS NOTHING
-- appointment one day late
#ASSERT `s 272(4)-(5) the company has complied with the direction` TRUE FALSE (JUST (Date 16 5 2024)) (JUST (Date 10 5 2024)) (Date 15 5 2024) (Date 17 5 2024) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- notice one day late, even though the appointment was in time
#ASSERT `s 272(4)-(5) the company has complied with the direction` TRUE FALSE (JUST (Date 10 5 2024)) (JUST (Date 16 5 2024)) (Date 15 5 2024) (Date 17 5 2024) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (5): the appointment was already made, so only the notice is needed
#ASSERT `s 272(4)-(5) the company has complied with the direction` FALSE TRUE NOTHING (JUST (Date 1 4 2024)) (Date 15 5 2024) (Date 2 4 2024) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 272(4)-(5) the company has complied with the direction` FALSE TRUE NOTHING (JUST (Date 15 5 2024)) (Date 15 5 2024) (Date 20 5 2024) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 272(4)-(5) the company has complied with the direction` FALSE TRUE NOTHING (JUST (Date 16 5 2024)) (Date 15 5 2024) (Date 20 5 2024) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 272(4)-(5) the company has complied with the direction` FALSE TRUE NOTHING NOTHING (Date 15 5 2024) (Date 10 5 2024) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 272(4)-(5) the company has complied with the direction` FALSE TRUE NOTHING NOTHING (Date 15 5 2024) (Date 16 5 2024) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- neither "Where the company is in breach" nor "If the company has already made the necessary appointment" holds: not covered
#ASSERT `s 272(4)-(5) the company has complied with the direction` FALSE FALSE NOTHING NOTHING (Date 15 5 2024) (Date 16 5 2024) EQUALS NOTHING

-- The same duty as a regulative rule (clock in days from the day the direction is given; the period ends 61 days later).
-- A #TRACE prints its outcome and moves no count; the outcomes are read from the run and recorded in NOTES.md.
-- (4): appointment on day 5 and notice on day 9, both inside the period: FULFILLED.
#TRACE `s 272(4) the company's duty as a regulative rule` 61 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company DOES `Action of a party` OF Company, Registrar, "make the necessary appointment (s 272(4)(a))" AT 5
    PARTY Company DOES `Action of a party` OF Company, Registrar, "give notice of the appointment (s 272(4)(b))" AT 9
-- (4): the notice comes on day 62, one day after the last day: BREACH.
#TRACE `s 272(4) the company's duty as a regulative rule` 61 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company DOES `Action of a party` OF Company, Registrar, "make the necessary appointment (s 272(4)(a))" AT 5
    PARTY Company DOES `Action of a party` OF Company, Registrar, "give notice of the appointment (s 272(4)(b))" AT 62
-- (5): the notice on the last day, day 61: FULFILLED; on day 62: BREACH.
#TRACE `s 272(5) the company's duty as a regulative rule` 61 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company DOES `Action of a party` OF Company, Registrar, "give notice of the appointment (s 272(5))" AT 61
#TRACE `s 272(5) the company's duty as a regulative rule` 61 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company DOES `Action of a party` OF Company, Registrar, "give notice of the appointment (s 272(5))" AT 62

-- ---- s 272(6): the offence ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- (a) the company commits an offence "if" it fails to comply with the direction (the answer of s 272(4)-(5) is the input).
#ASSERT `s 272(6)(a) the company commits an offence` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 272(6)(a) the company commits an offence` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 272(6)(a) the company commits an offence` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- the shadow director is treated as an officer
#ASSERT `s 272(6) a shadow director is treated as an officer of the company` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 272(6) a shadow director is treated as an officer of the company` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 272(6) a shadow director is treated as an officer of the company` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- (b) arguments: complied?, officer (s 1173(1))?, shadow director (s 251)?, in default (s 1121)?
#ASSERT `s 272(6)(b) the officer commits an offence` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a shadow director is treated as an officer even where s 1173(1) leaves the position open ("includes")
#ASSERT `s 272(6)(b) the officer commits an offence` (JUST FALSE) NOTHING (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- an officer who is not in default is outside "every officer of the company who is in default"
#ASSERT `s 272(6)(b) the officer commits an offence` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 272(6)(b) the officer commits an offence` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- a person who is neither an officer nor a shadow director is not named by the text
#ASSERT `s 272(6)(b) the officer commits an offence` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 272(6)(b) the officer commits an offence` (JUST FALSE) NOTHING NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- the company complied, so there is no offence for anyone ("If a company fails to comply ...")
#ASSERT `s 272(6)(b) the officer commits an offence` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- whether the company has failed is not yet settled
#ASSERT `s 272(6)(b) the officer commits an offence` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- s 272(7): the penalty -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- "liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 5 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily
-- default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 5 on the standard scale" (first wording), or "one-tenth of the greater of
-- £5,000 or level 4 on the standard scale" (second wording).
#ASSERT `s 272(7) the penalty on a person guilty of an offence under section 272` `on summary conviction` (JUST `s 272(7) one-tenth of level 5 on the standard scale`) EQUALS JUST (`s 272(7) penalty` OF `on summary conviction`, `a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 5 1, `s 272(7) a fraction of a level on the standard scale` 0.1 5)
#ASSERT `s 272(7) the penalty on a person guilty of an offence under section 272` `on summary conviction` (JUST `s 272(7) one-tenth of the greater of £5,000 or level 4 on the standard scale`) EQUALS JUST (`s 272(7) penalty` OF `on summary conviction`, `a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 5 1, `s 272(7) a fraction of the greater of an amount in pounds and a level on the standard scale` 0.1 5000 4)
-- a summary conviction in a named place is a summary conviction
#ASSERT `s 272(7) the penalty on a person guilty of an offence under section 272` `on summary conviction in Scotland` (JUST `s 272(7) one-tenth of level 5 on the standard scale`) EQUALS JUST (`s 272(7) penalty` OF `on summary conviction in Scotland`, `a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 5 1, `s 272(7) a fraction of a level on the standard scale` 0.1 5)
-- the text states the penalty only on summary conviction
#ASSERT `s 272(7) the penalty on a person guilty of an offence under section 272` `on conviction on indictment` (JUST `s 272(7) one-tenth of level 5 on the standard scale`) EQUALS NOTHING
-- the rendering does not say which wording applies
#ASSERT `s 272(7) the penalty on a person guilty of an offence under section 272` `on summary conviction` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- in pounds (illustrative: level 5 stands for 100,000 pounds and level 4 for 3,000 or 8,000 or 5,000)
#ASSERT `s 272(7) the most a person guilty of an offence may be fined on summary conviction, in pounds` 100000 EQUALS 100000
#ASSERT `s 272(7) the most the daily default fine may be, in pounds` (JUST `s 272(7) one-tenth of level 5 on the standard scale`) 100000 3000 EQUALS JUST 10000
-- second wording: the greater of 5,000 pounds and level 4, one-tenth of it
#ASSERT `s 272(7) the most the daily default fine may be, in pounds` (JUST `s 272(7) one-tenth of the greater of £5,000 or level 4 on the standard scale`) 100000 3000 EQUALS JUST 500
#ASSERT `s 272(7) the most the daily default fine may be, in pounds` (JUST `s 272(7) one-tenth of the greater of £5,000 or level 4 on the standard scale`) 100000 8000 EQUALS JUST 800
#ASSERT `s 272(7) the most the daily default fine may be, in pounds` (JUST `s 272(7) one-tenth of the greater of £5,000 or level 4 on the standard scale`) 100000 5000 EQUALS JUST 500
#ASSERT `s 272(7) the most the daily default fine may be, in pounds` NOTHING 100000 3000 EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- s 273(3): the bodies --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#ASSERT `s 273(3) the body is one of the bodies specified in subsection (3)` `s 273(3)(a) the Institute of Chartered Accountants in England and Wales` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 273(3) the body is one of the bodies specified in subsection (3)` `s 273(3)(b) the Institute of Chartered Accountants of Scotland` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 273(3) the body is one of the bodies specified in subsection (3)` `s 273(3)(c) the Association of Chartered Certified Accountants` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 273(3) the body is one of the bodies specified in subsection (3)` `s 273(3)(d) the Institute of Chartered Accountants in Ireland` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 273(3) the body is one of the bodies specified in subsection (3)` `s 273(3)(e) the Institute of Chartered Secretaries and Administrators` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 273(3) the body is one of the bodies specified in subsection (3)` `s 273(3)(f) the Chartered Institute of Management Accountants` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 273(3) the body is one of the bodies specified in subsection (3)` `s 273(3)(g) the Chartered Institute of Public Finance and Accountancy` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 273(3) the body is one of the bodies specified in subsection (3)` `s 273(3) any other body` EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ---- s 273(2): the qualifications ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- (a) "at least three of the five years"
#ASSERT `s 273(2)(a) the person has held the office of secretary of a public company for at least three of the five years immediately preceding the appointment` 3 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 273(2)(a) the person has held the office of secretary of a public company for at least three of the five years immediately preceding the appointment` 5 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 273(2)(a) the person has held the office of secretary of a public company for at least three of the five years immediately preceding the appointment` 2.5 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 273(2)(a) the person has held the office of secretary of a public company for at least three of the five years immediately preceding the appointment` 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (b) a member of any of the bodies in (3)
#ASSERT `s 273(2)(b) the person is a member of any of the bodies specified in subsection (3)` EMPTY EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 273(2)(b) the person is a member of any of the bodies specified in subsection (3)` (LIST `s 273(3) any other body`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 273(2)(b) the person is a member of any of the bodies specified in subsection (3)` (LIST `s 273(3) any other body`, `s 273(3)(a) the Institute of Chartered Accountants in England and Wales`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 273(2)(b) the person is a member of any of the bodies specified in subsection (3)` (LIST `s 273(3)(g) the Chartered Institute of Public Finance and Accountancy`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (c) a barrister, advocate or solicitor called or admitted in any part of the United Kingdom
#ASSERT `s 273(2)(c) the person is a barrister, advocate or solicitor called or admitted in any part of the United Kingdom` `s 273(2)(c) a barrister` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 273(2)(c) the person is a barrister, advocate or solicitor called or admitted in any part of the United Kingdom` `s 273(2)(c) an advocate` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 273(2)(c) the person is a barrister, advocate or solicitor called or admitted in any part of the United Kingdom` `s 273(2)(c) a solicitor` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 273(2)(c) the person is a barrister, advocate or solicitor called or admitted in any part of the United Kingdom` `s 273(2)(c) a solicitor` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 273(2)(c) the person is a barrister, advocate or solicitor called or admitted in any part of the United Kingdom` `s 273(2)(c) another calling` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (d) the directors' view of a person who holds or held another position or is a member of another body
#ASSERT `s 273(2)(d) the person is a person who appears to the directors to be capable of discharging the functions of secretary` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 273(2)(d) the person is a person who appears to the directors to be capable of discharging the functions of secretary` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (2): one or more of (a) to (d)
#ASSERT `s 273(2) the person has one or more of the qualifications` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 273(2) the person has one or more of the qualifications` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 273(2) the person has one or more of the qualifications` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 273(2) the person has one or more of the qualifications` (JUST FALSE) NOTHING (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 273(2) the person has one or more of the qualifications` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE

